      "checkpoint": {
        "id": "lobby_door",
        "name": "The Lobby Door",
        "objective": "Crack the lobby door to get inside the bank.",
        "type": "intermediate",
        "tension_target": "tense"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "removeTransition",
      "ref": {
        "from": "start",
        "to": "vault"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "addTransition",
      "transition": {
        "from": "start",
        "to": "lobby_door",
        "priority": 1,
        "gate": {
          "q": "has_key",
          "op": "==",
          "v": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "addTransition",
      "transition": {
        "from": "lobby_door",
        "to": "vault",
        "priority": 1,
        "gate": {
          "q": "lobby_cracked",
          "op": "==",
          "v": true
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "Added one intermediate beat, 'lobby', sitting between the casing anchor and the vault anchor: the crew has to get through the bank's lobby door before the vault is even reachable. It carries a tense target since a botched door job is where alarms start. No snapshot was set — 'has_key' is the only declared quality and it isn't a latching/pivotal value here, and quality ops aren't allowed at this stage. Note for the next stage: the existing start→vault transition still fires directly on has_key, so the transitions pass will want to rewire it to start→lobby→vault.",
  "ops": [
    {
      "kind": "addCheckpoint",
      "checkpoint": {
        "id": "lobby",
        "name": "The Lobby Door",
        "objective": "Get the crew through the bank's lobby door without tripping the alarm.",
        "type": "intermediate",
        "tension_target": "tense",
        "guidance": "The lobby is the funnel between the street and the vault floor. Guards on rotation, a locked service door, and a camera sweep that has to be timed. Whatever the crew does here should leave them either inside and committed, or sent back out to the street with the alarm hotter than before — either way the vault should stay out of reach until the door is behind them.",
        "motive_notes": null
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "Added an intermediate beat, The Sun Door, between The Ruins and The Inner Chamber: the party must solve the light-and-shadow puzzle to open the way inward. Tension target set to tense; torch_lit is snapshotted true so the puzzle's lighting state is consistent when the beat begins.",
  "ops": [
    {
      "kind": "addCheckpoint",
      "checkpoint": {
        "id": "sun_door",
        "name": "The Sun Door",
        "objective": "Solve the sun door puzzle to open the way into the inner chamber.",
        "type": "intermediate",
        "tension_target": "tense",
        "state_snapshot": {
          "torch_lit": true
        },
        "guidance": "The sealed sun door bears a disc of burnished gold ringed by channels cut for light and shadow. Pressure plates and mirrored slots suggest the door opens when the party casts the right shape of light at the right hour-mark. Let the players experiment; a wrong configuration can grind the stone and stir something beyond, but do not resolve the puzzle for them. Reward clever use of torches, water, or the desert sun, and let the door open only once the party commits to an answer."
      }
    }
  ]
}

{"summary":"Provisions the cast the story still needs: Vex's card (the crew's lockpick, present at the casing), a story-owned lorebook "Vault Job Lore" with entries for the bank, its vault and the vault key, and the group that plays the story. The Assistant/Arin/Ponticius cards, the Adolion book and the Sun Ruins Party group are left untouched; no persona is created.","ops":[{"kind":"createCharacterCard","name":"Vex","description":"Vex is the crew's lockpick: wiry, fast-handed, and the one who reads a door the way other people read a face. She talks in half-sentences and dry jokes, keeps her tools in a rolled canvas wrap, and never stands still in an open street. She is casing the city bank with the crew right now and has not yet laid a finger on the vault.","role":"The crew's lockpick — she reads the bank's locks and leads the way into the vault.","personality":"Restless, sardonic, professional. Allergic to standing in the open. Proud of her hands and prickly about being doubted.","scenario":"Vex and the crew are casing the city bank from the street outside, working out how to reach the vault.","first_mes":"*Vex leans against the lamppost across from the bank, canvas tool wrap bulging under her coat, and watches the front doors without ever quite looking at them.*

"Two guards on the floor, one on the mezzanine, and the mezzanine one keeps checking his watch," *she murmurs, without turning her head.* "That's a shift change at the top of the hour. Means about ninety seconds where nobody's watching the corridor to the back."

*She finally glances sidelong at you.* "So. We case it, or we stand here until somebody calls the watch on us? Your call. But I'm not opening anything until I know what's behind it.""},{"kind":"createStoryLorebook","name":"Vault Job Lore"},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The City Bank","keys":["city bank","bank","the bank"],"content":"The city bank is a stone-fronted building on a busy corner: a public floor with teller windows, a mezzanine with a single guard post, and a corridor at the back leading to the strongroom. Shift changes happen at the top of the hour, when the corridor briefly goes unwatched. The crew is casing it from the street.","constant":true},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The Vault","keys":["vault","strongroom","the vault"],"content":"The vault is the bank's strongroom at the end of the back corridor: a steel door with a twin-tumbler lock, thick enough that no amount of noise inside will carry to the public floor. It cannot be opened without its key — the lockpick work only gets the crew as far as the keyway.","constant":false},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The Vault Key","keys":["vault key","key","keys"],"content":"The vault key is a long brass twin-tumbler key, kept off the premises and carried by the bank's manager. Getting hold of it — by theft, bribery or trickery — is the whole point of casing the bank. Without it the vault stays shut.","constant":false},{"kind":"createGroup","name":"Vault Job Crew","members":["Vex"]}]}
